; Plan 04's RULE 4: the essence says it is part 1 of 2 and is the only
; part there is.
;
; "A split body with a missing part" is the plan's own example of a
; corrupt payload, and it is what a sequencer that dropped one meta event
; leaves behind: every surviving byte is well formed and the essence
; still cannot be put back together. The skeleton is derived, the header
; says "the residue would not decode", and `residue_corrupt` names it.
;
; The LANE and CONDUCTOR records survive the same file — they are one
; event each and were never split — so the verdict table still shows them
; matching. That is the honest reading: the file's records are intact and
; the document they described is gone.
(read)
(dump)
